    {
        "content": "<p>What should I do to get a better view of what's happening?</p>",
        "id": 590663840,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris C",
        "timestamp": 1777022510
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think the \"biggest\" reason thinks are acting weird is that actually the whole goal after the <code>equals ..... =&gt;</code> is closable just by <code>rfl</code>. So, they are definitionally equal. <code>rw</code> tries to close goals with reducible rfl, but <code>erw</code> tries to close goals with semireducible rfl. That means it doesn't actually /need/ to do any rewrites at all. <code>simp only []</code> also tries to close the goal when the two sides are semireducible equal. So all four of these are valid proofs after <code>equals (CategoryStruct.comp ((adj T).counit.app X) ((Functor.id (Kleisli T)).map f)) =&gt;</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">erw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">adj</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">counit</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">naturality</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">erw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>One useful way to get an idea of what's happening is the <code>show_term</code> tactic, which you can put before any other tactic. For instance, <code>show_term simp only []</code><br>\ngives</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">of_eq_true</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">eq_self</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">adj</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">counit</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">app</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">𝟭</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Kleisli</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">map</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>which you can maybe recognize as simp saying \"these are just two equal things\". And <code>show_term erw []</code> gives a similar <code>exact Eq.refl ((adj T).counit.app X ≫ (𝟭 (Kleisli T)).map f)</code>. But <code>show_term erw [← (adj T).counit.naturality]</code> gives the longer</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Eq</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mpr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">id</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">congrArg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Eq</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">symm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">adj</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">counit</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">naturality</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">))))</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Eq</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">refl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">fromKleisli</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⋙</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">toKleisli</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">map</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">adj</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">counit</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">app</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>so indeed it is using the rewrite you gave it.</p>",
        "id": 590713126,
        "sender_full_name": "Alex Meiburg",
        "timestamp": 1777036365
    },
